>> title: French Fries, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: potatoes, chips, fries, air fryer, basket, side
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: french-fries
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer chips, air fryer fries, basket chips, air fried french fries, chips from a raw potato
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: narrow — they are best in the first five minutes and merely good after fifteen, and a basket chip has no second fry to hide behind
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> capacity: 4 — one 5.7 L air fryer basket, roast, air fry
>> keeps: not at all — cold they go leathery, and a second pass dries them out rather than crisping them

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Raw potato, one layer, no soaking bowl and no pan of oil.

>> step: cut 3/8-in batons, rinse and dry hard, toss with oil
Cut @russet potatoes{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; peeled or not, in 3/8-in batons), rinse the starch off, dry them hard in a towel and toss in a #bowl{} with @sunflower oil{1%Tbs}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 20–24 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)oiled batons{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{22%min}, one layer.

>> step: toss the basket twice — an edge snaps when lifted out, not bends
Toss @&(~1)chips{} by shaking the basket twice.

>> step: salt hot in the same bowl
Toss @&(~1)chips{} with @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}, @malt vinegar{2%tsp}.

>> step: No 30-minute soak. Rinsed and dried, they brown and soften at once instead of drying to glass first — that is the loss.
The soak is what makes the plain file worth an hour and a half.
